Package: SIMP
Title: Symplectic Integrators for Monte-Carlo Proposals
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R:
    person("Gilles", "Colling", , "gilles.colling051@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Gilles Colling [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Gilles Colling <gilles.colling051@gmail.com>
Description: Symplectic integration of Hamiltonian systems and the Hamiltonian
    Monte Carlo proposals built on them. Explicit splitting schemes for
    separable Hamiltonians cover leapfrog, minimum-error two- and three-stage
    members, and the Yoshida order 4, 6, and 8 members generated from a single
    triple-jump composition, so the whole family shares one stepper and one
    coefficient source. The multistage coefficients can be adapted to a target's
    step band from an exact harmonic energy-error analysis, and a
    multiple-time-stepping (RESPA) integrator advances a split potential at two
    rates. A generalized (implicit) leapfrog handles non-separable Hamiltonians,
    as in Riemannian dynamics with a position-dependent mass. The steppers are a
    header-only, scalar-templated C++ core that other packages can link against,
    so they run under automatic differentiation as well as plain double
    precision.
